---
description: Exclusive overlay/status actions are one onAction, not parallel handlers
alwaysApply: true
---

# No duplicate action props

If several callbacks only differ by which value they write to the **same** discriminant (`openedModal`, `status`, etc.), they are **one** `onAction`, not parallel props.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — same state, three wrappers
<HeaderDrawerContent
  onClose={() => setOpenedModal("none")}
  onOpenSettings={() => setOpenedModal("settings")}
  onOpenInstallGuide={() => setOpenedModal("install-guide")}
/>

// ✅ GOOD
<HeaderDrawerContent onAction={setOpenedModal} />
```

Child calls `onAction("settings")` (or `"none"`, `"install-guide"`, …). Do not add `onOpenX` / `onClose` siblings that only set that union.
